-- title:
--   Algebraic over R[g] from finiteness over K(g)
-- statement:
--   Let $R$ be a commutative domain and $K$ a field that is a fraction field of $R$ (an $R$-algebra satisfying `IsFractionRing R K`), and let $F$ be a field equipped with compatible $R$- and $K$-algebra structures, so that $R \to K \to F$ is a scalar tower; all three carry types in one universe. Let $g \in F$, and assume that $F$ is finite-dimensional as a vector space over the intermediate field $K(g) =$ `IntermediateField.adjoin K {g}`, the subfield of $F$ generated by the image of $K$ together with $g$. The conclusion is that $F$ is algebraic over the $R$-subalgebra $R[g] =$ `Algebra.adjoin R {g}` of $F$, that is, every element of $F$ is a root of some nonzero polynomial whose coefficients lie in $R[g]$. Note that the base here is a subalgebra, not in general a field, so `Algebra.IsAlgebraic` is asserted for a ring base.
--
--   This is the standard fact that finiteness of $F$ over $K(g)$, with $K$ the fraction field of $R$, forces $F$ to be algebraic over the subring $R[g]$, obtained by clearing denominators. It serves to discharge the algebraicity hypothesis in the construction of normal proper models and of valuation-subring descriptions of local rings, and is used in the analysis of node charts on modular curves of full level.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_Algebra_IsAlgebraic_adjoin_singleton_of_finiteDimensional_intermediateField_adjoin_of_isFractionRing.lean

